# Production build config — THIS FILE IS COMMITTED TO GIT ON PURPOSE.
#
# Vite bakes env values into the bundle at BUILD time, and the local `.env` is
# gitignored, so it never reaches the host that builds the site. Without a key
# there, the deployed form correctly falls back to its "not configured" note.
# Keeping the key here means any host that runs `npm run build` from this repo
# picks it up automatically, with nothing to configure in a dashboard.
#
# This is safe: a Web3Forms access key is a PUBLIC token by design. It ships
# inside the JavaScript bundle that every visitor downloads, so it is readable
# from the live site whether or not it is in this repo. It is not a password —
# it only ever delivers mail to the one inbox it was issued for, and it grants
# no access to any account.
#
# To rotate it, request a new key at https://web3forms.com and update both this
# file and your local `.env`.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=7fd8745e-8361-4c3e-9e5e-4cd928a23640
